 3. For each uniq key: if slot_of.get → slot (ref_bit[slot]=true, pinned[slot]=true); else victim = victim() → map.remove(key_of[victim]);                 
    map.put(key→victim); key_of[victim]=key; pin+refBit... (slotstream: fill → scatter → eval; new slot is pinned until layer end? "hit → pin + refBit;    
    miss → pick victim → readBatch → scatter → eval" — misses are... in slotstream's Swift, ensure unpins at the start of the layer; within ensure the     
    victim slot gets refBit... hmm, slotstream's SlotPool.ensure(keys): "hit → pin + refBit; miss → pick victim → readBatch 9N preads → scatter per block  
    → eval". So misses: victim selection skips pinned + refBit; after fill, the new slot is probably pinned+refBit too (else a second key in the same      
    batch could evict the first key's slot — possible when n_slots < uniq count... n≥1152 and uniq ≤512 → can't happen, but for correctness on small pools 
    let's pin the miss too).                                                                                                                               
 4. Fill: pread 9×n_miss bytes (QD parallel) → wrap staging per piece as mlx array on s → scatter into pool array (slot idx array + updates) → eval → free 
    staging + free handles.                                                                                                                                
