 = 1.13 ms on a 5.66 GB pool, 0.00 GB of new allocations during scatter (vs 21.41 ms for a full-pool copy, 18.9×). In other words MLX's scatter is         
 in-place if the conditions are met (buffer donation = if is_donatable — if the source buffer's refcount permits, MLX donates/reuses the output buffer     
 instead of copying!). Prerequisite: "if the prerequisite is not met, it silently degrades to a full-pool copy" — that prerequisite = switch_* must not    
